This spreadsheet is a simple example of how to do an amortization
schedule using the Psion spreadsheet.  Given the user-supplied data at the
top of the spreadsheet (loan amount, term and interest), we calculate the
monthly payment required.  In the second section, we calculate up to 24
months of payments, breaking out the interest and principle components. 
Additional principle amounts can be entered in this section, and the rest
of the schedule will adjust accordingly.

Additional months of payments can be added by copying and adding lines to
the bottom of the second section.  (Note that I didn't make the payment
number a formula:  you'll have to adjust the payment number by hand. 
Sorry about that.)

Hope this proves useful to someone!

